{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Real-time visualization of MIDI Continuous Controller (CC) messages with two display modes: a scrolling time graph and current-value bars, plus performance metrics for hardware testing and technique analysis (events/s, rate, jitter).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each CC number is tracked per MIDI channel, so the same CC from different channels is displayed and measured separately.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Slider 1 selects the CC to monitor (0 = all CCs); slider 3 sets the time window in seconds (1-30). Metrics are computed over a 1-second rolling window.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 REAPER tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 My public REAPER tools, published as a {\b ReaPack repository} \u8212- install once, and REAPER keeps them up to date.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 In REAPER: {\i Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import a repository}, paste this URL, then synchronize:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/solyarisoftware/reaper/raw/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Manual install, if you prefer: copy the {\f1 .jsfx} {\b and} its {\f1 .jsfx-inc} companions into {\f1 Effects/MIDI/} inside your REAPER resource directory (on Windows {\f1 %APPDATA%\\REAPER\\Effects\\MIDI}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Packages\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | Type | Category | What it does | |---|---|---|---| | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "MIDI/midi_cc_visualizer.jsfx"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
MIDI CC Visualizer
}}}
 | JS effect | MIDI | Real-time graph and value bars of MIDI CC messages, per channel, with performance metrics |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 MIDI CC Visualizer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1738\pich1020\picwgoal26344\pichgoal15461 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Two display modes: a scrolling time graph and one bar per active CC. Each CC number is tracked {\b per MIDI channel}, so the same CC from different channels is shown and measured separately.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Slider 1} \u8212- CC to monitor ({\f1 0} = all CCs, {\f1 1-127} = one CC)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Slider 3} \u8212- time window, 1\u8211-30 s\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Metrics}, computed over a 1 s rolling window: {\b events/s} (message frequency \u8212- controller resolution), {\b rate} in units/s (how fast the values move \u8212- gesture intensity), {\b jitter} in ms (timing consistency \u8212- a hardware quality indicator)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 It was written for testing MIDI hardware: the numbers tell you whether a controller really transmits at high resolution, whether its timing is stable, and how hard you are actually moving it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 How this repository is organised\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This is a ReaPack repository, so {\b the folder tree is the package taxonomy}: a file in {\f1 MIDI/} is installed as {\f1 Effects/MIDI/<file>} and shows up under the {\i MIDI} category in ReaPack. The {\f1 index.xml} at the root is generated from the files' metadata headers by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
reapack-index
}}}
 running in GitHub Actions \u8212- do not edit it by hand.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Related repositories\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The scale collections are separate projects, each with its own documentation:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/solyarisoftware/Claude-Debussy-Scales"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Claude-Debussy-Scales
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/solyarisoftware/Alexander-Scriabin-Scales"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Alexander-Scriabin-Scales
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/solyarisoftware/Olivier-Messiaen-Modes"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Olivier-Messiaen-Modes
}}}
\sa180\par}
